{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>For.</b> This is astonishing: why does he not consider the toil of gathering wealth and not eating everything he desires — for who eats his wealth except him alone? The meaning is: is there anyone who is worthy to eat it like me? It is known that one who says <b>לבד</b> ('alone,' 'besides') means 'his matters are vanity,' and this thing alone departs from the general rule. Likewise the meaning of <b>חוץ</b> ('outside,' 'except'). And there is no language like this in Scripture, but only in the words of the early transmitters of the commandments, of blessed memory. And <b>ויחוש</b> means to hurry toward all his desire, like <i>מהרה חושה</i> ['she hurried, she hastened' (Judges 5:28)]."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Resolved ז״ל to 'of blessed memory' and embedded the Judges 5:28 quotation phrase as a parenthetical gloss to clarify the comparison."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:13.878411325Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}